      "id": "new-roman-empire-s007-p00617",
      "source_en": "Theodosius died in his late forties. The 390s witnessed the death of older men such as Libanios, Themistios, Ammianus, and Gregory of Nazianzos, men who had come of age in the vastly different world of Constantine and his heirs. After 395, without their living memory to anchor it in that past, eastern Rome embarked on a new phase of history that was defined by the reign of Theodosius and by developments in Christian culture.",
